What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/otp/target
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Read/write BIG hardware PID target in whole degrees Celsius.
		Range 50..150, default 150. Lowering the value reprograms the PID
		and resets the recovery interval. The actuator is CPUfreq maximum
		QoS, bounded by the manual OPP table and 2405000 kHz. It does not
		enable autonomous iDVFS or write CPU VPROC/VSRAM voltages.
		The cap relaxes after two continuous seconds at least 5 C below
		the target. BIG cluster OFF/ON and system PM reinitialize the PID.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/otp/state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Read-only PID configuration, active cap (kHz), score/frequency
		output, samples, failures and longest work interval (ns).
		The nominal sampling period is 5 ms; workqueue execution is not
		a hard real-time deadline. Read/access failures apply the minimum
		BIG cap. This is separate from the TC direct-reset final boundary.
